The dataset for this project is the  Online Retail II dataset from UC Irvine ML repository, found here: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/502/online+retail+ii

This project consists of a customer segmentation based on RFM (recency, frequency and monetary value) analysis using machine learning in Python. 
The model used is Kmeans clustering to cluster customers, and then posterior analysis is done to find the characteristics of each customer cluster, and based on the findings,
suggest actions or strategies to retain the customers and increase bussiness revenue. The data is cleaned and pre-processed as the dataset contains various invalid records and
qualities that are not specified in the website of origin.

This project is useful and impactful as this type of models can be used to make data driven decisions and find insights and value in data.
